<article class="doc">
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumbs.njk" %}
    <p class="micro">Support</p>
    <h1 class="doc-h">Something not working? Tell us.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>One developer builds this app, so whoever reads your message can fix
      it. Replies usually come within a couple of days.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Support%3A%20All%20Day%20I%20Dream%20About%20Sports">Email {{ site.email }}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{ site.issuesUrl }}/new">Report a bug on GitHub</a>
      </div>

      <h2>The ones we answer most</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>No alerts?</b> Follow the team, turn on the event types you
        want in settings, and check the right screen is picked. A short feed
        delay is normal.</li>
        <li><b>No notch?</b> Alerts drop just under the menu bar instead.</li>
        <li><b>Capsule in the way?</b> Drag it to another corner, or make it
        smaller in settings.</li>
        <li><b>Not running after a restart?</b> Turn on <b>Open at login</b>.
        The app lives in the menu bar, not the Dock.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>More answers in the <a href="/#faq">FAQ</a>, and the
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> covers your data.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
